-- title:
--   Gauss reduction of X₀(N) at a place above ℓ ∤ N
-- statement:
--   Let $N \ge 1$, let $\ell$ be a prime not dividing $N$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and assume `A.LiesOverPrime ℓ`, i.e. the image of $\ell$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $k =$ `IsLocalRing.ResidueField A`. Put $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull N` (itself the subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb Q$ the set `divisorExpansions N`), and put $\bar F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC k N`, the subfield of $k((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $k$ the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k\,d\,(j(q))$ for the non-zero divisors $d \mid N$. The assertion is that there exists a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to $F$ with residue field $\bar F$, that is: a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ whose intersection with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is exactly $A$, together with a surjective ring homomorphism $R.\mathrm{residue} : R.\mathrm{integers} \to \bar F$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and which restricts on $A$ to the residue map $A \to k$ followed by $k \hookrightarrow \bar F$, such that every non-zero $f \in F$ admits a constant $c \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $c \cdot f \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ and $R.\mathrm{residue}(c\cdot f) \ne 0$; and moreover $R$ may be chosen so that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image `coeffMap A.subtype y` in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ lies in $F$, that image lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, read inside $k((q))$, is the coefficientwise reduction `coeffMap (IsLocalRing.residue A) y`.
--
--   This is the Gauss, or $q$-expansion, reduction of the function field of $X_0(N)$ at a place of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ above a prime $\ell \nmid N$: the reduction is unramified over $A$ and its residue field is the full modular function field of level $N$ over the residue field, with residues computed coefficientwise on integral $q$-expansions. It is the input to the construction of the characteristic-$p$ fibre model of $X_0(N)$, and is used in particular for the identification of the $q$-expansion place after reduction and for producing integral lifts of the $j$- and $j$-invariant charts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_regularProlongation_modularFunctionFieldBar.lean

